5f2f151d7885962e201401c2468cd7152540326eAlexander Bandukwala2026-09-10T17:24:13-04:002026-09-10T17:24:13-04:00Document Typ.diff's cyclic-alias precondition

expanded_aliases is threaded through the two Var cases only; every other
case resets it, so a cycle passing through a Parens or Projector node
expands forever, and the recursive calls are in tail position so it
spins rather than overflowing. The old comment claimed a structural
descent always consumes a constructor from the left type, which is what
made the resets look safe.

