ddcbb32287c7e652b68ee01cb259b3aeb8be826aAlexander Bandukwala2026-09-10T15:04:15-04:002026-09-10T15:04:15-04:00test: turn the stats-only statics surveys into disabled property tests

The three `Slow` cases in Test_Statics_Properties.re counted how often a
property held and printed a distribution. None of them asserted, so a
regression in any of the three was invisible.

Each is now a real QCheck property wrapped in the `Alcotest.skip()` shape
already used for `Preservation of types (disabled)` in
Test_Evaluator_Properties.re, so the code stays compiled and re-enabling is
a one-line edit.

All three properties are false. `Elaboration preserves type` was the
surprise: its survey reported 1000/1000, but the survey seeded
`Random.State.make([|0xC0FFEE|])`, and QCHECK_SEED=1 fails. The other two
shrink to `(()) +. - []` (parent Float, fresh Int) and `{}`.

Dropped with the survey loops: two hand-rolled shrinkers that duplicated
each other and QCheck's own shrinking, the outcome variants the loops
tallied, and `show_exp`, which was a verbatim copy of
QCheck_Util.show_core_exp.

`show_core_typ` moves out of `arb_typ` to a top-level let beside
`show_core_exp`. Typ.show prints the whole IdTagged record, which rendered
a type disagreement as two ten-line blobs rather than Float vs Int.

