e626d0981468324b60c4901f3cf9bb767870b2d2Alexander Bandukwala2026-09-10T11:19:13-04:002026-09-10T11:19:13-04:00Call the coloured ids dynamic_ids, not marks

`Mark.t` is the error type -- `Info.typ` alone carries four `marks: list(Mark.t)`
fields -- so using "marks" for the ids of the runtime-derived parts of a type
put two unrelated concepts under one word in the same subsystem.

`dynamic_ids` is not a new coinage: the deleted `PadIds.compute_dynamic_ids`
was this codebase's own name for exactly this set, and it matches the existing
`error_ids` / `live_typing_error_ids` convention.

- `displayed_segment_and_marks` -> `displayed_segment_and_dynamic_ids`
- `Test_DynamicTypMarks.re` -> `Test_DynamicTypIds.re`
- local bindings, test names and comments now say green/coloured rather than
  marked

