95eb69d50e8718320b5465052b6e38c2069e9ab3Alexander Bandukwala2026-09-09T11:24:20-04:002026-09-09T11:28:22-04:00Replace Util.Either with result, and Core's Either where it is a partition

Our Either was `L | R` with show/sexp/yojson derivations that nothing
used -- no [@deriving] type in the tree embeds an Either.t. It also
shadowed Core's: every library using it has `-open Core` in its dune and
every file using it also does `open Util`, which lands second, so
Core.Either was unreachable unqualified.

Following the call sites, most of them were not partitions at all.
Operators and Atom returned `Either.t(value, InvalidOperationError.t)`
and Transition matched `L(return_value)` / `R(error)`: success-or-failure
spelled with constructors that do not say so. Those become `result`, so
the error direction is in the type rather than in a convention, and
MatchedTyp.args gets a concrete ok type (`list(Typ.t)`) instead of the
'a it carried.

Only Aba.split and its one caller Segment.split_by_matching genuinely
partition -- each element goes to the A-stream or the B-stream, neither
side an error -- so those take Core.Either's First/Second, and
src/util/Either.{re,rei} is deleted along with Util's re-export.

BuiltinsADT's own `Either` is the Hazel-language type alias and is
unrelated; it is untouched.

