32135e99587e471ce37ad9cb66071658280b5dceAlexander Bandukwala2026-08-21T12:46:17-04:002026-09-09T11:27:46-04:00Migrate src/web to Jane Street Core

Open Core over all four OCaml stanzas in src/web/dune -- the web and
workerServer libraries and the main and worker executables. 168 files,
+4413/-3982. Largest library so far: 223 files, 52k lines.

Mechanically similar to language: labelled arguments, Stdlib.* prefixes
for primitives Core deprecates or renames, and typed equality witnesses.
The 17 .ml/.mli example files under exercises/ and derivation/ are
compiled by the same stanzas and needed the same treatment -- 1245
Option.get call sites among them, since those files are generated and
full of Option.get (Id.of_string "...").

New total-vs-raising traps beyond the ones language hit:

  - String.index raises in stdlib and returns an option in Core.
    DerivationExercise's key parser *relies* on the exception, catching
    Not_found to terminate. Core's index_exn raises Not_found_s, which
    that handler would silently stop matching, so the parser uses
    Stdlib.String.index and Stdlib.Not_found -- exact behaviour rather
    than a plausible equivalent.
  - Point-free uses evade a paren-based sweep. List.map(~f=List.hd)
    in Backpack, and `|> List.hd` in DrvGrading and ExplainThis, kept
    type-checking as options; they are hd_exn now. Same for `|> List.split`.
  - Core's Option has `some` but no `none`, and does not re-declare the
    None/Some constructors, so Option.none and Option.None are unbound.
    Where the original wrote Option.None deliberately -- to disambiguate
    from another None in scope -- Stdlib.Option.none preserves that.

Equality follows the same split as language: name the witness where the
type is concrete (String.equal, Id.equal, Int.equal, Option.equal,
Direction.equal), leave int alone, and use Poly for structural comparison
of variants and records. Web leans on Poly much more than language -- 42
of 223 modules take `open Poly` -- because view and model code compares
whole variants and records constantly, and Poly is precisely the
semantics those comparisons already had. Files were selected by the
compiler: only modules whose failing line actually contains a comparison.

make test-quick stays at 3323 tests; release profile is warning-free.

Also corrects a comment in Transition.re that still named List.hd/List.tl
after the previous commit moved that call to the _exn variants.

