34aa565d271c832b6a469d0d4b1bf6bf46a2c6bdAlexander Bandukwala2026-08-21T10:46:41-04:002026-09-09T11:27:19-04:00Migrate src/util to Jane Street Core

Open Core in the util library and adapt all 43 modules to it. The library
is the atomic unit here: -open Core applies to the whole dune stanza, so
every module in src/util moves at once.

Wiring goes on the library stanza rather than in per-library env stanzas,
so `:standard` keeps inheriting the warning configuration that now lives
centrally in dune-workspace. `core` and `base` are already transitive
dependencies of bonsai.web, bignum, virtual_dom and incr_dom, so this
costs no additional bundle size.

The public API stays stdlib-shaped: Sets.re, Maps.re, MapUtil.re and Id.re
keep Stdlib.Set.Make / Stdlib.Map.Make / Stdlib.Map.OrderedType. Core's
comparator-based containers have a different interface -- add takes the
container first, cardinal becomes length, empty carries a comparator --
and src/language and src/haz3lcore call the stdlib shape. Converting those
belongs with the migration of their consumers, so nothing downstream of
src/util changes here.

The bulk of the diff is mechanical: labelling higher-order arguments
(~f, ~init, ~compare), the total-vs-exn split on List.hd / nth / map2 /
zip, and replacing polymorphic comparison with a typed equality or an
explicit Poly.equal where the type really is polymorphic. Reason's == and
!= elaborate to OCaml's = and <>, which Core restricts to int, so every
comparison on a string, char, float, list, option or variant needed an
explicit witness.

IntUtil.ipow keeps its hand-rolled loop. Core's Int.pow raises on a
negative exponent and on overflow where the loop silently wraps, and ipow
backs Hazel's ** operator, so swapping it would change language-level
behaviour rather than just implementation.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

ab1bffcf85aad31be18ccf8950e838985fa22a56Alexander Bandukwala2026-09-09T11:11:19-04:002026-09-09T11:17:25-04:00Say what these interfaces are, and give ~ancestors its real type

