c9e5723c55078a87be7cfec857e16a249fc77f9eAlexander Bandukwala2026-08-12T11:23:37-04:002026-09-09T11:10:46-04:00Add .rei interfaces for 13 leaf modules

These modules had no interface, so every helper in them was exported to all
485 modules in the build. Declaring only the surface that is actually used
across files removes 267 values from the public API for 24 declarations.

The public set was derived from the ocaml-index occurrence data (a value is
public iff some occurrence lies in another file), not from grep, so it matches
what scripts/find_dead_code.py already reasons about.

No dead code turned up, which is the expected result rather than a
disappointment: warning 32 is a hard error under --profile release, so a clean
build is positive confirmation that all 267 are used internally. src/ is still
at the index fixpoint.

WorkerMessagingSection.rei is just `include DebugSection.S;`, which moves its
contract check from the (module ...) pack site in DebugSidebar.re to the
definition itself.

Two things the interfaces surfaced, documented in place rather than fixed:

  - CustomStatics.custom_statics_deferred_ap discards ~ancestors, and its one
    caller (Statics.re:1751) passes a unit-typed pun where all eight other
    ancestors call sites in that file pass ancestors_inclusive. Annotating it
    list(Id.t) does not compile. Harmless while the parameter is discarded, a
    trap if anyone ever reads it.
  - Abbreviate.AbbrevBudget.split_evenly is exported only because
    Test_Abbreviate covers it directly.

