With Probe All on, every probeable site is sampled, and each sample
captured its full in-scope environment. Only the probe context menu
reads a sample's env, and on a ~150-line program with a few hundred
sites those per-sample env copies were ~80% of the retained heap
(worker 1.8 GB -> 186 MB after this change, measured on the aria-demo
circuit slide). Ambient sites now capture no env; explicit probes
(sites in probe_ids) keep theirs.

