422fe0450e54fd8072b2e82be61bb41c729817e0disconcision2026-09-07T20:01:10-07:002026-09-09T00:30:11-07:00Sampling while a definition cell is open: wells refresh in constellation mode

While a stack is open the master editor is frozen and only its RESULT
keeps evaluating the spliced program, but the master's `dynamics` field
(what the canvas wells and type-value tallies read) was never refreshed
from that result, so the wells showed pre-stack samples or nothing.
Refresh it from the stacked eval. Also: the stacked statics' targets now
recompute when probe_all toggles (they were computed once per stack);
turning probe_all on by hand releases the agent-burst mask; and while
probe_all is masked by a burst, one RefreshStatics is armed for the
moment the burst settles so ambient samples repopulate without an edit.

