444b1ac0be179d68b09be6457b554f2d61c8c133disconcision2026-09-08T10:19:09-07:002026-09-09T00:30:11-07:00Compositional statics: livelit uses and apps are probed for their live view

The monolithic path added dynamics-requesting projectors to the probe
set, so statics folded each livelit use's VIEW into the evaluation and
the projector rendered the sampled HTML. The per-item path passed only
the zipper's explicit probes, so no view sample ever existed and every
livelit rendered through the fallback that evaluates the raw model in
the builtin env — which stops working the moment an interaction leaves
`^name.update(prev, a)` in the syntax (^name is unbound there): after a
reload or any drop of the optimistic entry the widget showed the stuck
redex or "did not produce HTML" until re-expanded. Projector ids now
join the probe set on both the plain and the stacked path.

