46bdb6b16ecd6355864cbd879dddb4fdfbef67cfdisconcision2026-09-07T22:06:00-07:002026-09-09T00:25:26-07:00Compositional statics: spine roots carry the whole-suffix elab_term

The incremental evaluator reuses a node's previous result when its
elab_term is unchanged. Under the per-item engine the program's spine
roots (each `let … in`) carried the HOLLOW item elab (body = hole), so
the top root read as unchanged whatever happened downstream: an edit to
any definition but the first was never re-evaluated until an upstream
item changed. fix_spine_infos now grafts the suffix onto each root's
elab_term (the same term whole_elab builds; untouched subtrees are
shared). Regression test in Test_ModRoot.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Wor2U5BQAmt1XXaQj6do5f
(cherry picked from commit cbb6d81f543926ae144c12d055a55feb1626f000)

fb9c1aab4e08c2a6aa84d50405c7fefa285d3dc7disconcision2026-09-07T23:08:03-07:002026-09-09T00:23:12-07:00Ascriptions: an untyped constructor takes the sum it is ascribed to

Raw syntax fed to the evaluator without elaboration — a livelit's model
argument in the projector-side view/update path, an agent-inserted
value — carries constructors with no type. Ascribed to a sum that has
the constructor (the view's `m : Model`), the cast had no rule and
stuck, so every `case` on such a model was indeterminate: a livelit
whose model held program ADT values rendered its view unevaluated.
Two rules: a bare constructor takes the sum's type; an applied one
takes the arrow and pushes the ascription into its payload.

