f21ac5f8ddf1ee48f6977332d7bc275e675725d1disconcision2026-09-09T00:22:32-07:002026-09-09T00:22:32-07:00Ascriptions: resolve a constructor's own alias type before the consistency check

(cherry picked from commit 38e2ce821b; test moved to Test_Evaluator_Builtins)

`let j : JSON = Assoc(...)` and `let n : JSON = Null` stuck as casts:
since the compact builtin types (bce50ac5fc) a constructor's own type
is an alias of a recursive builtin sum, and the ascription rule only
unrolled it structurally, so the unrolled target never read as
consistent and every case on an annotated JSON binding stayed
indeterminate. Weak-head-normalize the constructor's type the way the
ascription's type already is. Not a dev bug (dev's rule uses structural
constructor types); the new test fails on this branch without the fix.

