c704c8149ffce1c5207dcc31bf2d9e04af3addbddisconcision2026-09-08T00:28:26-07:002026-09-09T00:19:15-07:00Worker: run the reuse pre-pass once, and only for large programs

Profiled a livelit drag on the graph slide: the worker spent ~1.2s of a
1.9s round trip in ReusePass (a full evaluation-shaped walk of the
program, run twice — once for the ReusePlan message, once inside
prepare_evaluation) and every evaluated node paid a reuse check, for a
~100-line program whose evaluation itself takes ~70ms. The plan's pass
now feeds the evaluation (one walk), and below 2500 statics entries the
request evaluates from scratch with no incremental cache. Measured
drag-to-result: ~2.0s -> ~0.45s (probe-all off), ~3s -> ~1.4s (on).
Large programs keep the incremental path unchanged.

