228342e51096ffe933bb07c20fe0403e5aeb31d2disconcision2026-09-09T00:13:59-07:002026-09-09T00:13:59-07:00Base-type keywords are constructor patterns; gate the marker end to end

Deleting the arrow in `let x : Int -> Bool` leaves a pattern-level
hole beside `Bool`, which lexes as a type keyword and had no pattern
production — so that document (and plain `let Bool = 1`) still hit
the recovering parser on every load. Exp already maps these tokens to
constructors; pat now does the same.

TextRoundtrip.EditedGrout: grout left by simulated typing, in every
sort, persists as text that fast-parses, keeps its grout through the
load-time regrout, and reprints as a fixed point.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Muw4jP1PUreZhEy3jWejKG

d1c3465369bcb3ab33e6c6c21159c1c0ce1379afdisconcision2026-09-08T22:52:44-07:002026-09-08T22:53:25-07:00Concave-grout marker in every sort, at the editor's precedence

The marker parsed only between expressions, and as the loosest infix
form — but the editor molds concave grout at Precedence.concave_grout
in Exp, Pat, Typ and TPat alike: looser than every operator, tighter
than `;` and the let/fun/if/case bodies. So `let x = 1 in x ⧖ 2`
fast-parsed as `(let …) ⧖ 2`, and any pattern, type or type-pattern
hole dropped the whole document to the recovering parser.

Grammar: CONCAVE_HOLE moves below the structural forms; pat/typ/
ascTyp/tpat productions and a fun-parameter chain; the arrow-bodied
binders (fun/fix/typfun, poly/rec) take a BINDER_BODY level so the
arrow token itself can sit tighter than the hole (`(Int -> Bool) ⧖
String`). AST BinHole{Pat,Typ,TPat}; Conversion flattens chains to one
MultiHole and prints uniform-sort MultiHoles back, as for Exp.

Pins: MenhirParser.ConcaveMarker (29 Menhir ≡ MakeTerm cases through
the marker load path) + 7 fast-parse round-trip cases. Unpinned by
design: the sort MakeTerm tags a hole's neighbour with, and Bool/String
lexing as type keywords (no constructor pattern there).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Muw4jP1PUreZhEy3jWejKG

