654c7929d6155ae90db964dab5a2b8c66a678e18Alexander Bandukwala2026-09-08T18:04:51-04:002026-09-08T18:05:07-04:00Merge hazel-html, adopting upstream's drawer over this branch's docking

Both branches had reworked where an open rich probe draws. This branch added
a renderer-level renderer_placement (modal over the code vs a card in the
Projectors panel, with ToggleRendererPlacement and a docked slot on the
projector view); hazel-html added drawer_mode with auto_rich/rich_off and a
below slot, opening the drawer when content exceeds inline_rows_cap.
Upstream's is the one kept, so:

  - probe_model takes drawer_mode / dropdown_redraw / auto_rich / rich_off and
    loses renderer_placement; the default is init_probe_model again
  - ProjectorBase.View gains "below" and loses "docked", so ProjectorView's
    docked_views and the panel's docked-probe pass go with it
  - the rich-probe view is upstream's rich_content / live_offside_view rather
    than this branch's modal plus dock button

renderer_placement was self-contained in ProbeProj (no external consumers), so
dropping it is local. What is NOT a competing design is the chart work itself:
HtmlRenderer stays registered alongside upstream's CardRenderer, and gains the
two members hazel-html added to the renderer signature -- auto_applies (HTML
and MVU apps are real evidence, so true) and drawer_rows (arbitrary-height UI,
so above inline_rows_cap and drawer-bound).

Also: mk_data took optional params upstream, so EditorCycle's call needs the
unit terminator, and Test_ShardCrashRepro's settings records need project_html.

