dea825d4cd7e3f4dbabe022239f95199feda7de4Alexander Bandukwala2026-09-08T17:50:20-04:002026-09-08T17:50:20-04:00Merge dyntype-proj (Probes IV) into dynamic_statics

The statics-refresh gate is the substantive resolution. This branch detected
probe changes by snapshotting multis.ephemerals around Editor.Update.calculate
and comparing; Probes IV replaced that with probes_differ, which compares the
zipper's probe ids against statics.targets directly and runs both before and
after calculate. That is strictly more general -- it catches any divergence
between the probe set and what statics recorded, whatever the cause, including
both cases the ephemerals check was written for (autoprobe cursor movement and
ephemerals rebuilt on reload) -- so the ephemerals snapshot is dropped. The
#2323 subset check does not apply here; it was only ever ported to oopsla2026.

The live-typing block (streaming throttle, filter_by_focus, live_typing_*)
now runs after the post-calculate refresh rather than before it, so it reads
the final statics. dynamics_map survives from this branch because the shared
Editor.Update.calculate call takes it.

Elsewhere Probes IV's shape changes drive the rest: CallStack.t is a plain
list again, add_sample gave way to record_event/ObsTrace.Minted (this branch's
RecordAscriptionProbe arm was duplicated by the merge; the ported one is kept),
EvaluatorState carries both this branch's type_insts and the new obs_trace, and
Arms takes ~simple_indication but not ~is_warning -- this branch's ~kind
variant already subsumes it, so the simple-arm classes go through shard_cls.

