Probes IV added sample-off-{text,bg,shadow} and simple-{error,warning}-backing
as literals in component CSS, so the slide could not reach them and they were
pinned to light-scheme values.

Each is now a role derived on the palette's own contrast axis, the same way the
sample-above/below/neutral triples already are. The wash factors reproduce the
light-scheme literals exactly (95.002%/84.9985%/71.998% against .95/.85/.72), so
light is unchanged; the other three schemes now follow instead of keeping a
lightness that only made sense on a white page -- sample-off-bg was 95% in every
scheme and is now 17.7% in dark.

The two backings sit at t < 0, a step outside the page background away from the
text, and are rotated onto the hues they replaced rather than the palette's reds
and yellows. They clamp to the background in contrast_dark, which has no room
below 0% -- the CSS literals stay as pre-slide defaults.

Golden gains 20 rows (5 names x 4 schemes) and changes none.

