d7adc2732f5223b761bd3bb1246a4f3c2f4cb9f5Alexander Bandukwala2026-08-12T10:29:21-04:002026-09-08T14:32:50-04:00Remove CSS rules for classes the compiled bundle never emits

Finishes the CSS pass using a stronger liveness test than the one behind the
previous commit: grep the compiled hazel.js. If a class name does not appear
anywhere in the 11MB bundle, no code path can put it on an element, so any
rule naming it is unreachable. Controls confirm the test discriminates rather
than trivially passing -- projector 108 hits, probe 256, hsod 9, depth- 4,
highlight-code- 1, agent-md-h 3.

That test says exactly 10 classes still defined in CSS can never be emitted,
and this removes their rules: developer-notes-display, view-icon-button,
deselected, call-cursor, click-kbd-pill, is-index, qr-when-unfocused,
window-toggle, step-back, step-expand. Nine were rules the previous pass
deliberately spared because their KEY selector is an element
(`.step-back:hover span`) -- unreachable all the same, since nothing carries
.step-back.

call-cursor is a correction. I kept it last time because `call_cursor` exists
in source, but that is a function name; the hyphenated class is never emitted.
The source-grep test was wrong and the bundle test is right.

Where a rule mixed dead and live selectors, only the dead branches are
dropped: `.prompt-display, .developer-notes-display` keeps .prompt-display,
and the .kbd-badge/.click-kbd-pill pair keeps .kbd-badge. One of those trims
initially took the rule's leading comment with it, because the dead branch was
listed first and carried the preceding trivia -- restored.

Verified in the browser, which also covers the earlier CSS commits and the
assistant.css/project.css deletion from the start of this branch. Walked probe
sidebar (incl. #sample-focus-bar with a focused sample, and probe hover cards
with kbd badges), agent panel, agent main menu, nut menu, editor context menu,
stepper (took a step), tutorial mode (completed a step, checkmark renders),
exercises mode with its grading reports, and the projectors slide. No console
errors, no unstyled surfaces.

The projectors slide also exercised the SliderProj/SliderFProj functor from
earlier in this branch end to end: both sliders render, and dragging each one
writes the literal back without failing -- the cursor inspector reads
"Projector (Slider) : Int" and "Projector (SliderF) : Float". That is the
runtime path the compiler could only check the signature of.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

259af265555f2b877f35c28f95b2a3df23fc4321Alexander Bandukwala2026-08-25T16:00:55-04:002026-09-08T14:32:50-04:00Match interfaces to dev: Unicode rework, clipboard Effects

dev's Unicode overhaul (#2393) reshaped Unicode.re — Width lost
