Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

78ed30877250fdb7e31555b9b5e63fa15191c721Alexander Bandukwala2026-08-11T16:02:42-04:002026-09-08T14:32:50-04:00Remove dead CSS rules and unreferenced assets

22 rule blocks (135 lines) across 9 stylesheets, 12 unreferenced icons, and
style/palette.html -- a design swatch page nothing links to and no dune rule
copies into the build.

This is the one change in the cleanup that no compiler can check, so the
liveness test is deliberately over-cautious. A selector counts as LIVE if any
of the following holds:

  - its name appears as a string literal anywhere in src/ or test/
  - some literal is a prefix of it, since classes get concatenated:
    "depth-" ++ string_of_int n, "agent-md-h" ++ string_of_int level,
    "highlight-code-" ++ c, "slash-card-" ++ kind
  - its name appears as a bare OCaml token. Sort and cls constructors reach
    the DOM through show/to_string and never appear as a literal at all, which
    is what .Mod, .Sig, .MPat, .Rul, .EmptyHole and .Single are. A naive
    literals-only scan called all of those dead.

That took the candidate list from 72 names to 22, and each of the 22 was then
re-checked by hand with a direct grep for both the hyphenated and underscored
spelling. .call-cursor was dropped from the list on that check -- there is a
call_cursor in source.

A rule is removed only when EVERY comma-separated selector is dead, judging by
the key (rightmost) compound: `.projector.probe .window-toggle` can only match
an element carrying .window-toggle, so it goes even though .projector is live.
Rules whose key compound is an element selector are left alone
(`.step-back:hover span` survives), which leaves a few orphans behind but
cannot break anything.

licenses/Icons.md is a blanket Noun Project attribution rather than per-icon,
so removing unused icons does not affect it.

NEEDS A BROWSER PASS, together with the assistant.css/project.css deletion
from earlier in this branch. Rebuild, restart the browser (a stale Web Worker
survives a hard reload), then check the probe sidebar, agent panel, agent main
menu, stepper, tutorial mode and the CSV projector.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

a64652c9c7eab21c15179abae1a2b8bdc2915dd1Alexander Bandukwala2026-08-17T15:55:54-04:002026-09-08T14:32:50-04:00Export JsUtil.print_timestamp

