b893c76262d00d6c2833ea60e9640ebdab687ccbdisconcision2026-09-07T19:24:08-07:002026-09-07T19:24:08-07:00DefStatics: livelit binders keep the monolithic item path

The member-granular module path (merged with modular-editors on 09-05)
runs a `let x = {...} in` wrapper on a `(hole : ty)` surrogate. For
`let ^name = {...}` the Let case then classifies a hole as the livelit
definition: InvalidLivelitDef on the let, no LivelitEntry, and every
use rendered "No livelit found" in the web (the CLI and tests use
monolithic statics, so nothing red-flagged it). Exclude livelit binders
from the surrogate path; parity test against monolithic statics.

