761a8c7f2fb9ec2025f7cc18e7857f8da71e28ccMatthew Hammer2026-09-05T21:55:59-06:002026-09-05T21:55:59-06:00Recover when the Fumola runtime finishes loading

The runtime is several megabytes of wasm, usually fetched cross-origin, so a
program is routinely elaborated before it exists. Such a program is not
wrong -- its Fumola livelits expand to "the runtime is still loading", which
was true when it was said -- but nothing ever revisited it. The card stayed
that way for the life of the page, and since card 0 is the one a cold
visitor lands on, that is the state they saw.

Three things were in the way, and each had to be moved:

  The shim never said anything. It now dispatches an event once the outcome
  is settled -- on failure too, so the message can settle from "still
  loading" to "unavailable" rather than waiting on a load that is not
  coming.

  Statics are rebuilt only for an edit. There was no edit, so the listener
  sets the same force_on_next flag the modes set for RefreshStatics, and
  sends Refresh to make a calculate pass happen at all.

  Elaboration is memoized on the term, and the term did not change. This is
  why forcing statics was not enough, and why editing the card did not help
  either: an unedited zipper yields an equal term and hits the cache. So the
  memo key now carries a generation, and the listener bumps it. Core.Memo
  has no way to clear an entry, which is why the key carries this instead.

Verified by making the race deterministic -- an artificial delay before the
runtime is published to the page -- and watching a card go from "the Fumola
runtime is still loading" to (6, 42, "adapton(settings)") on its own, with
no reload and no edit. Instrumented once to confirm all three fire in order:
the callback, then StaticsForce, then a recompute at the new generation.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

5f182c86b535905ea73749172fdc7f97c6236409disconcision2026-09-05T20:47:41-07:002026-09-05T20:47:41-07:00statics: a capitalized name resolves to its most recent binding, constructor or module

`module Text = { let f = fun n -> "x" } in Text.f(0)` reported "Expected a
tuple" whenever ANY constructor named Text was in scope: a capitalized name
parses as a constructor and was looked up constructor-first, falling back to a
variable only if no constructor of that name existed. So a module named like a
constructor lost to it regardless of which was bound later. Now the most recent
binding of the name wins, whichever kind (Ctx.newest_var_or_ctr) — ordinary
lexical shadowing, extended across the two kinds. Expression position only;
constructor patterns are unchanged.

Found by modular-editors' mega corpus (a module named Text) against a branch
whose HTML builtins define a Text constructor.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>

aaeae5dd8659b662007b14e10bbf3fbeccd24a62Matthew Hammer2026-09-05T21:34:28-06:002026-09-05T21:34:28-06:00Merge #2504: load the Fumola runtime from a list of sources
9812b724cfe0b3f585fad9e56e5f009f7039d89cMatthew Hammer2026-09-05T21:24:08-06:002026-09-05T21:24:08-06:00Load the Fumola runtime from a list of sources, not one

The Fumola Pages site is moving to fumola.org, and the move cannot be
made atomically from this side. Giving a Pages site a custom domain
makes its old URL 301 to the new one, and a redirect response carries no
Access-Control-Allow-Origin -- which a cross-origin import must have on
every hop of the chain, not merely on the last. So the published URL
this file hard-coded works before the switch and not after, and the new
one works after and not before.

Neither URL spans it; a list of both does, from either side. The local
build stays first, so working on Fumola and Hazel together is unchanged.
Once the domain has settled, the adapton.github.io entry only ever
redirects and can be dropped.

The chain becomes a loop, which is also how it reports what it tried
when every source fails, rather than only the last error.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

e0a612f6ce59d606ded89e39f7e2099e8f0ece70Matthew Hammer2026-09-05T20:51:18-06:002026-09-05T20:51:18-06:00Cards: say four livelits, since four are listed

Every Fumola card opens with the same reminder, and it counted three while
