Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

3c04a7dcb06db6326a8034edf3b1b4f08616d2c7Matthew Hammer2026-09-05T20:51:18-06:002026-09-05T20:51:18-06:00Card 0: Fumola in one card, before the eight that take it apart

The series explains Fumola an idea at a time, which works if you already
know what Fumola is. Someone opening the Fumola cards cold got values,
symbols and cells before anything said what the language is for.

So: a map, drawn from how adapton.github.io/fumola tells it, cut to fit a
couple of screens. What Adapton is -- a run leaves a graph of cells and
thunks, and the next run repairs that graph rather than redoing it, which
only works because every node has a name. The whole primitive set, which
is short: two ways to make a node, two ways to depend on one, peek to look
without depending, and a space to allocate in. Names as first-order data,
so a name can be computed. The archivist/editor split, which is what the
two main livelits are, and the graphical/simple split, which is what a
runtime chooses.

Three livelits carry it, one per claim, so the card runs rather than only
asserts: gcd through a named thunk, a put and a get in editor mode, and a
composed symbol. Verified live -- 6, 42, "adapton(settings)".

Numbered 0 so the existing eight keep the numbers they have.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

b24d0f4a4b9d450475cf5c24f307adbc18afebc2disconcision2026-09-05T19:00:54-07:002026-09-05T19:00:54-07:00statics: a newer variable binding shadows a same-named constructor

A module named like a builtin constructor (our HTML ADT has `Text`) lost
to the constructor at its use sites: `Text.f` typed the module name as the
constructor and reported "Expected a tuple". The newest binding of a
capitalized name now wins (Ctx.newest_var_or_ctr), which is what lexical
shadowing means. Found by modular-editors' mega-corpus test after the
merge; the corpus names a module Text. Also keeps the node-map/module
regression probes as a test group.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>

1f28cb8dc6f6c34bcb257e58fa759e3b837385bedisconcision2026-09-05T17:56:14-07:002026-09-05T17:56:14-07:00Merge origin/modular-editors (97cbeb3489) into agent-canvas

Outline sidebar, stacked per-definition editors, per-item statics
(DefStatics), incremental parse/measure (MakeTerm.Incr, Measured.Incr),
sparse remold/regrout. Resolution map: plans/agent-canvas-docket.md
"Modular-editors merge". Notable choices:

- Measured taken from modular-editors wholesale (chunked), with two
  canvas-side corrections: indentation is EXPLICIT here (rows start at
  column 0; their implicit level offset double-counted our indentation
  spaces and shifted every caret/decoration on indented rows), and a
  row's indent is its measured content start (Printer/Highlight/extreme
  moves read it as "where the text begins"). Compat accessor
  find_shards_by_id for refactor-drag tracks and FLIP staging.
- CachedSyntax: their m_cache/t_cache + our refractor rows (probe
  drawers) through the incremental re-measure.
- CachedStatics: our fingerprint ring/offers + their compositional init;
  the backpack test became a missing-shards test (canonical completion
  when shards are missing).
- CodeWithStatics: their gate/memo with our burst mask, offered statics
  and refractor-aware flat view (view_chunked awaits refractor rows).
- The agent tool path stays on MONOLITHIC statics: HighLevelNodeMap.build
  walks Info.ancestors to the program top and the per-item map records
  them per item (build = None). Converging the tools onto per-item
  statics is the next step.
- FocusEffect gains CellTop; ScratchPersist gains adopt_new_defaults;
  Settings/Page/CodeEditable/Arms/Init carry both sides' additions.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>

