c44507fd8837a0001bda029794d966288b1e69aedisconcision2026-09-05T02:17:33-07:002026-09-05T11:48:30-07:00agent: module members insert one at a time; compound forms never take an Any mold

Inserting several module members in one chunk parsed the chunk at Mod
root (so the `;` is the member separator) and the incremental typing
parse mis-molded the later members' case-rule patterns: the rule tiles
got an Any operand mold with no inner sort, and MakeTerm indexed past
`in_` — Failure "nth" reached the agent as the tool result four times in
the dungeon run. Now: insert_member splits the chunk at depth-0 `;` and
