eb546ce6629602954b2d00e120c0871549f0ef16Matthew Hammer2026-09-04T18:34:00-06:002026-09-04T18:34:00-06:00Render a Fumola reference as a widget

A translated pointer is now wrapped in a projector, so it draws as a widget
showing the cell being read and what it held, rather than as tokens.

The investigation was most of the work, and the first answer was wrong. I
thought this needed a new read-only projector-capable viewer, because
CodeViewable renders with an empty shape map and a projector piece then comes
out as blank space -- the widget itself is drawn by a layer positioned over
that gap. But results are not rendered by CodeViewable: EvalResult builds a
CodeSelectable model, which delegates to CodeEditable, which already draws
projectors. So the whole path existed, and a viewer I had written for this
was deleted unused.

What was needed was only that the value carry a projector. ExpToSegment
already turns a term-level Projector into a projector piece, so wrapping the
reference is enough.

The projector renders entirely from its own model, which carries both halves
as text. That is deliberate: a projector that had to consult statics would
find none where this one appears. The model type lives in language, shared
with the translation that builds it, for the same reason ProjectorKind does
-- the value is built below haz3lcore and cannot look up at it.

The kind is not in livelit_projectors and returns None from the projector
catalog: it is never chosen by a user, only produced by translation.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

