edce3b76bf781641eb6c00f2961b167f7fbd4ab7Matthew Hammer2026-09-04T17:14:15-06:002026-09-04T17:14:15-06:00Add Space and Time to the prelude, shaped as Fumola defines them

    type Space = + Symbol(String) + Here
    type Time  = + Symbol(String) + Now

Each is mostly just a symbol -- a name for a place, or for a moment -- with
one case that is not: `here` and `now` are relative to where evaluation is
and name nothing. A symbol arrives in Hazel as its text, so that is what the
Symbol case carries.

Fumola's Space has a third case, an expression rather than a name. It is left
out deliberately: nothing on this side has a use for it, and a value carrying
one fails to translate rather than arriving mis-shapen.

With these, Adapton's own introspection comes across whole. Adapton.peekEvents
is a list of records carrying event variants, spaces, times and edge ids;
before, it failed on its contents.

One thing to watch: Space and Time both declare a Symbol constructor. Where
an expected type says which is meant, translation resolves it correctly;
without one it falls back to a context lookup that could pick either.

Adapton/fumola#46 is merged, so the published runtime carries this and a
checkout with no local wasm build gets it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

