15b7dd1b7906204fcf14d3897e4c7c03038ab98aMatthew Hammer2026-09-04T16:52:29-06:002026-09-04T16:52:29-06:00Give a fumola_thunk an explicit, stable thunk name

Its model becomes (instance, thunk name, program). The name is Fumola source
for a symbol, parsed by Fumola itself, so `myThunk, 7 and `a(`b) all work and
Hazel needs to know about none of them.

Written by the programmer rather than derived, which is the point. The name
was taken from the livelit's Hazel id, and that id is not established to be
stable across edits: if it changed, an edit would start a new thunk and
quietly lose the history the thunk exists to keep. An explicit name cannot
drift.

The editor livelit keeps its (instance, program) model, having no thunk to
name.

Also documents all three things this branch adds -- the two livelits and the
peek value form -- in docs/livelits.md, the in-app documentation slide, and
the cursor inspector.

Needs Adapton/fumola#46.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

