a04a632add268bb25f7b2c074f43edd2bfbfdde1Matthew Hammer2026-09-04T15:18:36-06:002026-09-04T15:18:36-06:00Translate a Fumola pointer into the livelit that reads it

A pointer becomes a fumola livelit over the same instance, running
get(<the name it points at>). So a livelit that returns a pointer returns a
simpler livelit.

    `counter := 41   ->   ^fumola(<same id>, "get(`counter)")

The term is inert where it lands, and that is worth being clear about:
statics splices an expansion in without traversing it, so a livelit inside
one is never expanded, and widgets come from projectors over editor syntax,
which an expansion is not. What this gives is a faithful reading of what a
pointer is -- not a value, but the expression that would fetch one -- and the
displayed form doubles as the code to follow it. Copied into a program it
becomes a real livelit.

Needs Adapton/fumola#46 for the AdaptonPointer tag.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

0957bdc6302977f479e9d98e6d2ada1eec935362disconcision2026-09-04T14:15:28-07:002026-09-04T14:15:28-07:00canvas: traces — self-contained runs, a store, a pausable replay with marks, and a hidden panel

