8dd99f2567d9e0902868b722b9aec5bd270437ecMatthew Hammer2026-09-04T11:47:28-06:002026-09-04T11:47:28-06:00Load the Fumola runtime from its published build, not a committed binary

The runtime is now published to GitHub Pages from the Fumola repo
(Adapton/fumola#45), so Hazel no longer carries it. Nothing binary is
tracked in this repo any more; a checkout with no local build falls back to
https://adapton.github.io/fumola/ and works, which I verified by removing
the local copy entirely.

Pages rather than a release asset, deliberately: release downloads carry no
Access-Control-Allow-Origin header, so a browser cannot fetch one. Pages
serves the file with CORS and as application/wasm.

The glue and the .wasm are always taken from the same place, since
wasm-bindgen generates them together and they will not load if their
versions disagree. Building locally is now only needed when working on
Fumola and Hazel together.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

6f6e0ac5760db83c77a4c8ff4ba7b7796e8f1153Matthew Hammer2026-09-04T11:22:41-06:002026-09-04T11:22:41-06:00Document the Fumola livelit prelude

Programs now run after a prelude defining pointer(s), get(s) and peek(s),
because Hazel strings cannot contain the quotes the adapton primitives need,
